\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Reality does not choose a sign}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The [finite connection sum](fdip-00TU) is defined even
with signed weights. A positive mass does not by itself force
every determinant of #{m\bbI+\extD_U} to be positive.
What does the single-loop sign model give, and which operator
bound is sufficient for a nonnegative connection law?}
